                                "sense_id": "d914d7cf-6051-30e0-9d0c-1ac4cad8a769",
                                "text": "Moją ulubioną techniką rysunkową jest niezmiennie sangwina."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eab63e49-c846-4799-a3fe-8b867a145665",
                        "source_entry_id": "bdf2e480-e316-32d5-8e1e-7e90d677a6bb",
                        "source_sense_id": "d914d7cf-6051-30e0-9d0c-1ac4cad8a769",
                        "target_lang_word": "invariably",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "invariably",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9db3b003-4636-30c5-b137-10af909a7f88",
                                        "entry_id": "ccc78c6c-c7f0-3d92-ae84-2f3450102f52",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Every time; always, without change."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4554fa52-4683-4c42-9403-d7de31b6f978",
                                                "sense_id": "9db3b003-4636-30c5-b137-10af909a7f88",
                                                "text": "He is invariably late for meetings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30578225-9071-47fb-b134-b2b161ca9fd0",
                                                "sense_id": "9db3b003-4636-30c5-b137-10af909a7f88",
                                                "text": "“A tight little craft,” was Austin’s invariable comment on the matron;[…]. ¶ Near her wandered her husband, orientally bland, invariably affable, and from time to time squinting sideways, as usual, in the ever-renewed expectation that he might catch a glimpse of his stiff, retroussé moustache."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0091b6e-119e-4c97-b924-ddcd6b28fc24",
                                                "sense_id": "9db3b003-4636-30c5-b137-10af909a7f88",
                                                "text": "In common with most Swiss Railways the standard of equipment and of operating efficiency is high, and stations and trains are invariably clean and well maintained."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3cfe3b9-3b96-4d74-8c8a-a8524260f294",
                                                "sense_id": "9db3b003-4636-30c5-b137-10af909a7f88",
                                                "text": "As a consequence of the previous rules, each of the sixty-four squares is invariably indicated by a unique combination of a letter and a number."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cde6cef1-c17e-42c4-abca-6078d656fbdb",
                        "source_entry_id": "bdf2e480-e316-32d5-8e1e-7e90d677a6bb",
                        "source_sense_id": "d914d7cf-6051-30e0-9d0c-1ac4cad8a769",
                        "target_lang_word": "unalterably",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "unalterably",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4be688b3-c0d8-37eb-b539-22690d3be52e",
                                        "entry_id": "2d92228a-9630-33ef-9652-56e78dd89cac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an unalterable manner; in a manner that makes it impossible to be altered."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8f9b866-296b-4b49-8b40-f632dfe05425",
                                                "sense_id": "4be688b3-c0d8-37eb-b539-22690d3be52e",
                                                "text": "First experiences are always the most memorable because they fix themselves in the mind unalterably and most powerfully."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ce63089-d44e-4b49-868a-2146c50c7d38",
                                                "sense_id": "4be688b3-c0d8-37eb-b539-22690d3be52e",
                                                "text": "Sac. From that instant my affection was unalterably fixed on him—and thence I am reduced to my present langour."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a624330e-c096-4d3f-887b-da2ebd90eed2",
                        "source_entry_id": "bdf2e480-e316-32d5-8e1e-7e90d677a6bb",
                        "source_sense_id": "d914d7cf-6051-30e0-9d0c-1ac4cad8a769",
                        "target_lang_word": "unchangeably",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "unchangeably",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43645cc4-7160-3487-b55e-11c889aabf96",
                                        "entry_id": "586673a5-48dd-3f78-9639-d3c741481faf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a way that cannot be varied, or changed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "539d4fad-ca7a-4759-8955-6a0b1572f832",
                                                "sense_id": "43645cc4-7160-3487-b55e-11c889aabf96",
                                                "text": "God is infinitely and unchangeably good."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "39426c80-a62a-4f15-b97e-dbd72528aac7",
                        "source_entry_id": "bdf2e480-e316-32d5-8e1e-7e90d677a6bb",
                        "source_sense_id": "d914d7cf-6051-30e0-9d0c-1ac4cad8a769",
                        "target_lang_word": "fixedly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fixedly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ae7b57e-b805-31bf-bc2b-b071cffa3086",
                                        "entry_id": "87711aef-e770-37b1-85de-640f7989f1e6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a fixed manner.",
                                            "Firmly, resolutely."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "279d5edd-4dd2-4cd9-bfbb-cf22ee6802a4",
                                                "sense_id": "6ae7b57e-b805-31bf-bc2b-b071cffa3086",
                                                "text": "And ſhall not the vvant of Reaſon and Speech, be a ſign to us of different real Conſtitutions and Species, betvveen a Changeling, and a reaſonable Man? And ſo of the reſt, if vve pretend, that the diſtinction of Species is fixedly eſtabliſhed by the real Frame, and ſecret Conſtitutions of Things."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78bb3d5f-4ed9-4f62-b523-fb808c4d620c",
                                                "sense_id": "6ae7b57e-b805-31bf-bc2b-b071cffa3086",
                                                "text": "It vvas his manner in the Morning to meditate very ſeriouſly and fixedly upon ſome Truth, or ſome Text, for a good part of an Hour together."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b76c0ba-646c-4d6d-9261-3b3fbd12fcad",
                                                "sense_id": "6ae7b57e-b805-31bf-bc2b-b071cffa3086",
                                                "text": "But the difficulty of the circumstances in which he was placed was so great, that it was almost impossible for him to make up his mind fixedly to any purpose in reference to Clara."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2f89379-bf6d-4c66-b264-6db24423c0cc",
                                                "sense_id": "6ae7b57e-b805-31bf-bc2b-b071cffa3086",
                                                "text": "I am by no means sure that it [the rhinoceros] had fixedly hostile intentions, and indeed with my present experience I think it likely that if I had not fired it would have flinched at the last moment and either retreated or gone by me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73148cfe-78ff-4ab5-ab28-9223dfa452e4",
                                                "sense_id": "6ae7b57e-b805-31bf-bc2b-b071cffa3086",
                                                "text": "That is my view of the position, but if the Under-Secretary will agree with me we will certainly take the opportunity of discussing this in the course of conferring with the noble Lords who raised the point. I do not suppose anybody has made up his mind fixedly."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a001e98-c296-3357-9bb7-4aae5939daf4",
                                        "entry_id": "87711aef-e770-37b1-85de-640f7989f1e6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a fixed manner.",
                                            "Without changing one's expression; unchangingly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48b99372-0f6a-4e55-86a4-4efcc14e9ff7",
                                                "sense_id": "9a001e98-c296-3357-9bb7-4aae5939daf4",
                                                "text": "A consultation has been held in the corridor or in the washroom. Rhonda is smiling fixedly. Lonnie H. is looking wise and sad."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c16d6fa-2d6b-3302-a58f-d738caab1712",
                                        "entry_id": "87711aef-e770-37b1-85de-640f7989f1e6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a fixed manner.",
                                            "Without shifting one's gaze; intently, steadily."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89d30262-a71b-4978-a4de-fbd14445164a",
                                                "sense_id": "6c16d6fa-2d6b-3302-a58f-d738caab1712",
                                                "text": "She look'd as if ſhe vvould devour me vvith her eyes, ſtaring at me from head to foot, vvithout the leaſt regard to the confuſion and bluſhes her eyeing me ſo fixedly put me to, and vvhich vvere to her, no doubt, the ſtrongeſt recommendation, and marks of my being fit for her purpoſe.",
                                                "translation": "Fanny Hill",
                                                "english": "Fanny Hill"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98b970fd-896a-4b3a-b05f-1e9b36c91695",
                                                "sense_id": "6c16d6fa-2d6b-3302-a58f-d738caab1712",
                                                "text": "But when I turn away, / Thou, willing me to stay, / Wooest not, nor vainly wranglest; / But, looking fixedly the while, / All my bounding heart entanglest, / In a golden-netted smile; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f644290-49d5-4f9d-a344-4f9c1ee30ef9",
                                                "sense_id": "6c16d6fa-2d6b-3302-a58f-d738caab1712",
                                                "text": "The old man [William Kiffin] looked fixedly at the king [James II of England], burst into tears, and made answer, \"Sir, I am worn out; I am unfit to serve your Majesty or the City. And, sir, the death of my poor boys broke my heart. That wound is as fresh as ever. I shall carry it to my grave.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33b51af5-0fb0-4751-b69e-6eba8a996166",
                                                "sense_id": "6c16d6fa-2d6b-3302-a58f-d738caab1712",
                                                "text": "Did you fixedly gaze, too, upon that ribbed and dented brow; there also, you would see still stranger foot-prints—the foot-prints of his one unsleeping, ever-pacing thought."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87a332c6-fb9e-440b-b04f-98824344dc1f",
                                                "sense_id": "6c16d6fa-2d6b-3302-a58f-d738caab1712",
                                                "text": "He felt alone in the room and looked up, and there, grey and dim, was the bandaged head and huge blue lenses staring fixedly, with a mist of green spots drifting in front of them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1aaf574b-0798-46f7-9135-3e1b42ae3a62",
                                                "sense_id": "6c16d6fa-2d6b-3302-a58f-d738caab1712",
                                                "text": "By looking fixedly at the page, he hoped to make him move on; by pointing his finger at a word, he hoped to recall his mother's attention, which, he knew angrily, wavered instantly his father stopped."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "41ca191a-cc94-4e36-8c51-24e2033f01b3",
                        "source_entry_id": "bdf2e480-e316-32d5-8e1e-7e90d677a6bb",
                        "source_sense_id": "d914d7cf-6051-30e0-9d0c-1ac4cad8a769",
                        "target_lang_word": "immutably",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "immutably",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2910c484-35fd-392f-a9b8-9dd498ae6fb7",
                                        "entry_id": "4cbbe950-577d-381e-8172-1512c2007c5b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an immutable manner. In a way that cannot be varied, or changed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "362ae07d-dbb1-4086-a3ef-644b4df7e407",
                                                "sense_id": "2910c484-35fd-392f-a9b8-9dd498ae6fb7",
                                                "text": "My task was a very hard one; but, as I was absolutely resolved - as my cousins saw at length that my mind was really and immutably fixed on making a just division of the property....they yielded at length."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dc4ce051-67df-4454-ad1d-af6de74cfb3d",
                        "source_entry_id": "bdf2e480-e316-32d5-8e1e-7e90d677a6bb",
                        "source_sense_id": "d914d7cf-6051-30e0-9d0c-1ac4cad8a769",
                        "target_lang_word": "immuablement",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "immuablement",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc52243c-7262-3417-a30a-f3ecafcf8914",
                                        "entry_id": "5eb9fd32-be93-3fa0-9c6f-1f1452dd75b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "D’une manière immuable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "655cf3b1-8b48-4af6-b3d9-01b3ad8dd852",
                                                "sense_id": "dc52243c-7262-3417-a30a-f3ecafcf8914",
                                                "text": "Jésus-Christ a donné une nouvelle forme au mariage, en réduisant cette sainte société à deux personnes immuablement et indissolublement unies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04a2b273-bb54-4437-ad5b-85dc9af1ebc2",
                                                "sense_id": "dc52243c-7262-3417-a30a-f3ecafcf8914",
                                                "text": "La charité est consommée, quand elle est immuablement unie à Dieu sans pouvoir en être séparée."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58cb326d-56d3-4930-8187-0c8c531f9e2e",
                                                "sense_id": "dc52243c-7262-3417-a30a-f3ecafcf8914",
                                                "text": "Il serait à désirer que ces autres dépôts [de dépêches] fussent placés aussi sûrement et aussi immuablement que l’est celui de la guerre."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3007cc1a-fd23-47fa-9a41-c72ab4a34af9",
                                                "sense_id": "dc52243c-7262-3417-a30a-f3ecafcf8914",
                                                "text": "Xénophon, dans l’éloge qu’il nous a laissé d’Agésilas, et Cicéron, dans une de ses harangues, remarquent que Lacédémone était la seule ville du monde qui eût conservé immuablement sa discipline et ses lois pendant un si grand nombre d’années."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fb0655a-0fc4-4def-97a1-c9fcd66b2dbc",
                                                "sense_id": "dc52243c-7262-3417-a30a-f3ecafcf8914",
                                                "text": "Et celle-ci, soumise, obéissant aux files rigides et aux quinconces rigoureux, nourrit la proportion immuablement consacrée de 4400 ceps à l'hectare."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d41c0d2e-fb72-47f1-b14d-024cd757a9fe",
                        "source_entry_id": "bdf2e480-e316-32d5-8e1e-7e90d677a6bb",
                        "source_sense_id": "d914d7cf-6051-30e0-9d0c-1ac4cad8a769",
                        "target_lang_word": "invariablement",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "invariablement",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cdaebe22-fba3-3149-860b-37e6fd604742",
                                        "entry_id": "27a5e193-1599-352a-b302-5901093a78c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "D’une manière invariable ; d’une façon constante."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "304bc3d3-87fb-4cad-9529-47291540f97f",
                                                "sense_id": "cdaebe22-fba3-3149-860b-37e6fd604742",
                                                "text": "C’étaient invariablement les mêmes essences, des pins, des sapins, des saules, dont la présence attestait, dans cette terre froide, une certaine force végétative."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb00d2a0-da89-48fd-8ad5-cf5273b31721",
                                                "sense_id": "cdaebe22-fba3-3149-860b-37e6fd604742",
                                                "text": "Apparemment conçu pour que personne ne s’y attarde, sauf les chauffeurs-gardes du corps venus déposer et attendre leurs ministres qui assistent au Conseil ou à diverses autres réunions, ce hall ne comporte aucun véritable endroit pour s’asseoir, à l’exception de deux longues banquettes de bois peu invitantes et sur lesquelles traînent invariablement colis et enveloppes en attente d’un messager ou d'un taxi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf57720a-8c48-4387-a5f9-fb48d742b784",
                                                "sense_id": "cdaebe22-fba3-3149-860b-37e6fd604742",
                                                "text": "C'est chez la veuve Thorsdal que j'appris à savourer les délices de la cuisine islandaise. Le dîner se composait invariablement de poisson bouilli."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b81036d2-6665-47f2-8fad-2312c3fd778c",
                                                "sense_id": "cdaebe22-fba3-3149-860b-37e6fd604742",
                                                "text": "Invariablement les fonctionnaires, arrivés récemment ici des autres parties de la France, éprouvent de l’étonnement en voyant ces classes drues, ces hordes de galopins qui déambulent par les routes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "450e3708-f9c7-431c-943f-5779e0804477",
                                                "sense_id": "cdaebe22-fba3-3149-860b-37e6fd604742",
                                                "text": "Il m’était impossible de rester cinq minutes avec elle, qu’une dispute —qui se terminait invariablement par des violences de sa part— n’éclatât aussitôt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce7ce49e-5ae5-4c8f-bf6b-a8abef00abfd",
                                                "sense_id": "cdaebe22-fba3-3149-860b-37e6fd604742",
                                                "text": "Je l’ai vu en photo, sur un canapé en velours, tapotant de la main sur l’accoudoir, avec ses cheveux invariablement blancs et son air de pythie grecque assise sur les fumerolles de l’île de Ré."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
